f the spending is on substations and transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. The sources give no absolute capex figures.\n- **Equity issuance:** Pellham withdrew its planned C$2.4B equity offering because investor demand fell short. It will now cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. Two utility share offerings were also cut back in size in Q3 2026.\n- **Debt versus equity:** Debt is open but costlier. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. So Norvane, at +12%, looks able to fund through debt, while Pellham's equity route failed.\n- **Valuations, P/E and dilution capacity:** I found no P/E, share price or market-cap data, so I can't quantify dilution capacity. The failed and downsized deals are indirect evidence that investors will not absorb large issuance at current prices.\n\n**Implication:** Expect some 2027 grid equipment orders to be cut, mainly Pellham's transformers (about 40%). Debt-funded Norvane is less exposed. This conflicts with a pure demand-growth view, such as the one in n2's result.","ttft_ms":3498,"type":"result","duration_ms":22082,"uuid":"9a8d827c-4c88-4c37-8db8-1fd6d8d90b67","ttft_stream_ms":2889,"time_to_request_ms":524,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":51,"system_prompt":21,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":16,"input_attachments":87,"input_hooks":14,"conversation_append":18,"transcript_persist":65,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":39,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":13,"message_prep":11,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":50,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":20,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":20,"client_creation":13,"request_build":48},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":261,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":85,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":197,"process_a